# Nightly Needs you sweep (sd:9764): `sd reports sweep` (pack sd:9759)
# closes what Today's Attention list holds but no longer needs the
# operator: an alert whose condition cleared, a question already answered,
# a followup whose item is done. Each close gets a note naming why; a row
# it cannot prove stays open. Its lines (what closed, what could not) land
# in logs/needs-sweep-nightly.log and the run's report.
#
# Hub only: it writes the hub's database. machine-setup's cron stage
# installs it on the hub with no profile line (SD_HUB_ROLE_SEEDED).
# 07:50 local: after the night's jobs have filed their alerts, before
# night-triage at 08:40 reads what is left.
# SD_PACK_ROOT is escaped so the `bash -c` that runs the command reads it,
# after ~/.config/shell/env.sh; this file is sourced before env.sh is.
JOB_SCHEDULE="50 7 * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="10m"
JOB_COMMAND="\"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}/bin/sd\" reports sweep"
